<title>USA: Frankfort First Q3 March 31 net falls.</title>
<headline>Frankfort First Q3 March 31 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFORT, Ky. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in Thousands)  (Unaudited)</p>
<p>					     Nine months   Three months</p>
<p>					   1997	1996   1997   1996</p>
<p> Provision for losses on loans	 5	  9	0	3</p>
<p> Net Earnings			    463    1,295    307    359</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share		   0.15     0.41   0.10   0.11</p>
<p> Dividends Per Share		  0.27     0.27   0.09   0.09</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said lower earnings for the current quarter were caused by reduced balance of average interest-earning assets, which fell to $126.5 million from $136.6 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>The company also said the reduction is due to a one-time charge of $13.8 million for capital paid to stockholders on June 3, 1996.</p>
<p>Current nine-month period includes one-time charge of $567,000 to recapitalize its Savings Association Insurance Fund.</p>
<p>Full name is Frankfort First Bancorp Inc.</p>
</text>
